# Day 51

## Experiment Title

Integrating GitHub with Jenkins


## Objective

To understand how GitHub repositories can be integrated with Jenkins for Continuous Integration.


## Theory

Jenkins can integrate with GitHub repositories to automate software development workflows. Whenever code changes are pushed to GitHub, Jenkins can automatically trigger build and testing processes.

This integration improves development efficiency and ensures faster feedback during application development. GitHub integration also helps automate Continuous Integration tasks effectively.


## Requirements

Jenkins

GitHub Repository

Java Development Kit

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the Jenkins dashboard.

Create or configure a Jenkins project.

Connect the GitHub repository with Jenkins.

Configure repository access and build triggers.

Save the project configuration.

Push changes to the GitHub repository and observe Jenkins build execution.


## Output

GitHub repository integration with Jenkins was completed successfully.

Jenkins automatically detected repository changes and executed the build process.

Build logs and execution details were displayed successfully.


## Result

Successfully integrated GitHub repositories with Jenkins for Continuous Integration.
